1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-0--0a-method-overview","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-0/0a-method-overview","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-0/0a-method-overview","sourceHash":"40082136a824a81d4926cf90b582bda9261ea89dffc00ed25a0fa78321dad329","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:30.573Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"0A — Method Overview","zh":"0A — 方法概览"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Before diving into your language learning journey, here's a quick tour of what you'll be working on in each phase. Every phase has specific details, activities, and other useful information in the rest of the roadmap.","zh":"在开始语言学习之旅之前，先快速了解一下每个阶段要学习的内容。路线图的其余部分会详细介绍每个阶段的具体内容、活动以及其他有用信息。"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There are 7 main phases on your pathway to fluency:","zh":"通往流利程度的路径共有7个主要阶段："}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Foundations","zh":"基础"},{"en":"Comprehension","zh":"理解能力"},{"en":"Listening","zh":"听力"},{"en":"Speaking","zh":"口语"},{"en":"Accuracy","zh":"准确性"},{"en":"Fluency","zh":"流利度"},{"en":"And Beyond","zh":"以及更进一步"}]},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The names describe the primary goal of each phase, but each one has more to it than the name implies.","zh":"这些名称描述了每个阶段的主要目标，但每个阶段包含的内容都比名称所暗示的更多。"}},{"id":"phase-1-foundations","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 1: Foundations","zh":"第1阶段：基础"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The primary learning approach for the entire Refold method is immersion in the language and comprehending things. This allows your brain to learn patterns and develop fluency subconsciously. But you must actually <em>comprehend</em> things in order to learn.","zh":"整个 Refold 方法的主要学习方式，是沉浸于目标语言并理解所接触的内容。这能让你的大脑学习语言模式，并在潜意识中培养流利度。但你必须真正<em>理解</em>内容，才能学会。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>How do you understand <em>anything</em> if you're a beginner?</strong> You might ask.","zh":"初学者如何理解目标语言中的任何内容？你可能会问。"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"That's what the foundations phase is for. You'll use basic vocabulary and grammar study alongside simple content to slowly turn the gibberish that is your target language into... less gibberish. You still won't understand much by the end, but the language will stop feeling overwhelming and foreign.","zh":"这就是基础阶段的作用。你会将基础词汇和语法学习与简单内容结合起来，逐渐把目标语言中仿佛毫无意义的声音变成……没那么难懂的内容。到阶段结束时，你仍然不会理解太多，但这门语言不再让你感到不知所措和陌生。"}},{"id":"phase-2-comprehension","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 2: Comprehension","zh":"第2阶段：理解能力"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once you don't feel like you're drowning in the language, you want to increase your comprehension as quickly as possible. The easiest way to do that is to start with reading. It's generally much easier than listening and lets you use your adult literacy skills to make rapid progress.","zh":"当你不再觉得自己快被语言淹没时，就要尽快提高理解能力。最简单的方法是从阅读开始。阅读通常比听力容易得多，还能让你运用成年人的读写能力快速进步。"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"However, you won't be ignoring listening. Through the entire comprehension phase, we recommend you only read <em>along with</em> audio. This trains your ears to hear the language instead of relying solely on text.","zh":"不过，你不会忽视听力。在整个理解能力阶段，我们建议你只<em>配合</em>音频进行阅读。这能训练你的耳朵去听懂目标语言，而不是完全依赖文字。"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"When we say \"reading,\" we don't just mean books. Anything with text counts. Some of the best resources during this phase are TV shows and YouTube videos with subtitles which match the audio.","zh":"我们所说的“阅读”并不只是读书。任何包含文字的内容都算。这个阶段最好的资源包括带有与音频匹配字幕的电视节目和 YouTube 视频。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of the comprehension phase, you'll be able to understand things (when reading) at a fairly high level — far ahead of any traditional learner at the same hour count.","zh":"理解能力阶段结束时，你将能够以相当高的水平理解（阅读时）各种内容——在相同学习时数下，远远领先于任何传统学习者。"}},{"id":"phase-3-listening","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 3: Listening","zh":"第3阶段：听力"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Focusing on reading first creates a \"reading-listening gap,\" where your reading ability is well ahead of your listening. This means two things: you'll feel a sudden drop in ability when switching to listening-only, but you'll improve very rapidly as your ears catch up. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-reading-listening-gap\">The Reading-Listening Gap</a>","zh":"先专注于阅读，会形成“读听差距”，即你的阅读能力远远领先于听力。这意味着两件事：切换到纯听力时，你会感觉能力突然下降；但随着耳朵逐渐跟上，你也会进步得非常快。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-reading-listening-gap\">读听差距</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It can be uncomfortable to suddenly understand a lot less than you did a few days ago. But the fact that you already know so much from reading means that as your ears adjust, everything clicks into place quickly. That's what this phase is focused on.","zh":"突然比几天前少理解很多内容，可能会让人不舒服。但你已经通过阅读掌握了大量内容，因此耳朵一旦适应，一切就会迅速融会贯通。这正是本阶段的重点。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Towards the end of this phase, you'll turn your focus to conversations and pronunciation, preparing you for speaking.","zh":"在本阶段后期，你会将重点转向对话和发音，为口语阶段做准备。"}},{"id":"phase-4-speaking","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 4: Speaking","zh":"第4阶段：口语"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It might seem like writing would be easier to start with, since you can take your time and think. But that causes <em>overthinking</em> and gets in the way of building speaking fluency.","zh":"由于可以慢慢来并进行思考，你可能会觉得从写作开始更容易。但这会导致<em>想得过多</em>，妨碍口语流利度的培养。"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You'll start with specific exercises to make sure you're comfortable producing the sounds and rhythm of the language, as well as mentally preparing for a first conversation.","zh":"你会先进行一些特定练习，确保自己能够自如地产生这门语言的声音和节奏，同时为第一次对话做好心理准备。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This preparation matters because you'll be able to <em>hear</em> a lot of your own mistakes and awkward phrasings — you've spent so much time on input that your ear is far ahead of your mouth. This can be frustrating when you're just trying to speak. So the first focus is getting over that initial difficulty and speaking a lot. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-input-output-gap\">The Input-Output Gap</a>","zh":"这种准备很重要，因为你会<em>听到</em>自己许多错误和不自然的表达——你投入了大量时间进行输入，因此耳朵远远领先于嘴巴。刚开始说话时，这可能会令人沮丧。所以第一步是克服最初的困难，多说多练。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-input-output-gap\">输入与输出的差距</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0022","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There's an optional sub-phase for practicing specific situations (travel, daily life, work) which can be done at any point. If you have a specific use for your target language or are going on vacation, this is very valuable. But it's not required for the overall method.","zh":"还有一个可选的子阶段，用于练习特定场景（旅行、日常生活、工作），可以在任何时候进行。如果你有明确的目标语言使用需求，或即将去度假，这会非常有价值。但它不是完整方法的必需部分。"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end of the speaking phase, you'll be able to have a real conversation with a native speaker. You'll still have mistakes, but you'll be well on your way to fluency. Roughly equivalent to reaching B1. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR Levels</a>","zh":"口语阶段结束时，你将能够与母语者进行真正的对话。你仍然会犯错，但已经稳步走在通往流利的路上。大致相当于达到 B1 水平。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR 等级</a>"}},{"id":"phase-5-accuracy","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 5: Accuracy","zh":"第5阶段：准确性"}},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"After getting over the initial hurdle of speaking comfort, the focus shifts to accuracy. Writing is the perfect tool for this — you can take your time, look things up, and study grammar to make sure you're not just understandable, but correct. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-cara-model-for-output\">The CARA Model for Output</a>","zh":"克服开口说话的最初障碍后，重点会转向准确性。写作是实现这一目标的完美工具——你可以慢慢思考、查找资料并学习语法，确保自己不仅能被理解，而且表达正确。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-cara-model-for-output\">CARA 输出模型</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"You'll use your writing and grammar study to improve your speaking too, slowly reducing errors and unclear phrasing.","zh":"你会利用写作和语法学习来改善口语，逐渐减少错误和不清晰的表达。"}},{"id":"segment-0027","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"By the end, you'll be comfortable speaking and writing roughly around the level of a native high school student in the language. Roughly equivalent to reaching B2.","zh":"到最后，你会自如地使用口语和书面语，大致达到该语言母语高中生的水平。大致相当于达到 B2 水平。"}},{"id":"phase-6-fluency","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 6: Fluency","zh":"第6阶段：流利度"}},{"id":"segment-0029","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once you're comfortable and fairly accurate, all that's left is increasing your fluidity and naturalness. This phase is about developing automatic use of the language, filling gaps in your knowledge, and doing lots and lots of practice.","zh":"当你表达自如且相当准确后，剩下的就是提高语言的流畅性和自然度。本阶段旨在培养语言的自动化运用能力，填补知识空缺，并进行大量练习。"}},{"id":"segment-0030","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The general goal of the Refold method is to reach \"functional fluency,\" meaning you can live your life entirely in the language without it drastically impacting your ability to function. You can have a social life, hold a job, navigate the world, and enjoy media. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">Functional Fluency</a>","zh":"Refold 方法的总体目标是达到“功能性流利”，也就是说，你可以完全用这门语言生活，而不会严重影响自己的正常生活能力。你可以拥有社交生活、从事工作、应对日常世界并享受媒体内容。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/functional-fluency\">功能性流利</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0031","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Finished Phase 6 is roughly equivalent to reaching C1.","zh":"完成第6阶段大致相当于达到 C1 水平。"}},{"id":"phase-7-and-beyond","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Phase 7: And Beyond","zh":"第7阶段：以及更进一步"}},{"id":"segment-0033","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once you're fluent, your journey doesn't stop. You're now a user of the language and it's become part of who you are. During the following years, you'll continue to read, write, listen, speak, and learn so much more.","zh":"达到流利后，你的旅程并不会停止。此时你已经成为这门语言的使用者，它也已经成为你身份的一部分。在接下来的岁月里，你会继续阅读、写作、听力、口语，并学习更多内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0034","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"But there are specific things you can do to deepen your fluency purposefully. You can focus on becoming an expert in certain domains, or put yourself through the kind of learning that native speakers do during their years of schooling.","zh":"不过，你可以通过一些具体方式有意识地深化流利度。你可以专注于成为某些领域的专家，或进行母语者在求学过程中所经历的那类学习。"}},{"id":"segment-0035","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Phase 7 is technically never-ending — a lifelong journey of discovery and learning.","zh":"第7阶段在理论上永无止境——这是一次终身探索与学习之旅。"}},{"id":"skill-progression","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Skill Progression","zh":"技能进阶"}},{"id":"segment-0037","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Refold method develops your skills in a non-standard order. The CEFR scale assumes reading, listening, writing, and speaking all progress at roughly the same rate. That doesn't happen with this method.","zh":"Refold 方法以非标准顺序培养你的技能。CEFR 量表假定阅读、听力、写作和口语大致以相同速度进步，但这种方法并非如此。"}},{"id":"segment-0038","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Our approach is more of a \"cascade,\" meaning that one skill follows another. We find that it's more efficient to focus on one thing at a time (just reading, then listening, etc) rather than trying to do it all at once. You're able to focus better on the skill at hand and then use that ability to make faster progress in the next skill you turn your focus to.","zh":"我们的方法更像是一种“级联”，也就是说，一项技能接着一项技能发展。我们发现，与其试图同时面面俱到，不如一次专注于一件事（先只阅读，再听力，依此类推），效率更高。这样你能更好地专注于当前的技能，然后利用这项能力，在下一项技能上更快取得进展。"}},{"id":"segment-0039","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Here's the approximate progression if you were to follow the exact Refold method: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR Levels</a>","zh":"如果你完全按照 Refold 方法学习，大致会经历以下进展：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/cefr-levels\">CEFR 等级</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0040","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Phase","zh":"阶段","header":true},{"en":"Reading","zh":"阅读","header":true},{"en":"Listening","zh":"听力","header":true},{"en":"Writing","zh":"写作","header":true},{"en":"Speaking","zh":"口语","header":true}],[{"en":"1","zh":"1","header":false},{"en":"A2","zh":"A2","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false}],[{"en":"2","zh":"2","header":false},{"en":"B1","zh":"B1","header":false},{"en":"A2","zh":"A2","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false}],[{"en":"3","zh":"3","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"B1","zh":"B1","header":false},{"en":"A1","zh":"A1","header":false},{"en":"A2","zh":"A2","header":false}],[{"en":"4","zh":"4","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"A2","zh":"A2","header":false},{"en":"B1","zh":"B1","header":false}],[{"en":"5","zh":"5","header":false},{"en":"C1","zh":"C1","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false}],[{"en":"6","zh":"6","header":false},{"en":"C1","zh":"C1","header":false},{"en":"C1","zh":"C1","header":false},{"en":"B2","zh":"B2","header":false},{"en":"C1","zh":"C1","header":false}],[{"en":"7+","zh":"7+","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0041","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<em>Note: passing an official CEFR test will almost certainly require some study of the test structure and format, regardless of your actual ability.</em>","zh":"<em>注意：无论你的实际能力如何，通过官方 CEFR 考试几乎肯定都需要针对考试结构和形式进行一些准备。</em>"}},{"id":"refold-is-not-a-dogma","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Refold is not a Dogma","zh":"Refold 不是教条"}},{"id":"segment-0043","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"A rule we've had in our learning community since day 1 is that Refold is not a dogma. The Refold Method is meant to be a framework that you can build your own learning system on top of.","zh":"从学习社区成立第一天起，我们就一直遵循一条原则：Refold 不是教条。Refold 方法旨在成为一个框架，你可以在此基础上构建自己的学习系统。"}},{"id":"segment-0044","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"If you want to ignore our recommendations or change things, you should! We try to be general with our suggestions, but each person is different and has different learning needs.","zh":"如果你想忽略我们的建议或进行调整，那就去做吧！我们会尽量让建议具有普适性，但每个人都不同，学习需求也各不相同。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
